# Flutter + flutter_rust_bridge Debugger Spike Report

> **Status: PASS at flutter_rust_bridge 2.13.0-beta.4 + Flutter 3.44.4.**
> Earlier this report declared frb web "not viable" under 2.11.1 / 2.12.0 — **superseded** by this update. 2.11.1 and 2.12.0 stable still fail (see test matrix); the stable fix has not shipped.

## TL;DR

The frb web build works in `flutter_rust_bridge 2.13.0-beta.4`. The blocker in stable (2.11.1 / 2.12.0) is a one-line signature mismatch between the Dart loader and the wasm-bindgen-generated JS shim. The spike also shipped two downstream fixes (a `StaticTable` widget for unbounded-height contexts and a `build_live` empty-state gate) — both were copy-paste debt from before the rinf spike fixed them. All four tabs (Overview / Questions / Traces / Live) are now vision-verified end-to-end.

## Test matrix

| Flutter | frb | result |
|---|---|---|
| 3.44.4 | 2.11.1 | **FAIL** — `DataCloneError` at `worker_pool.rs:254` |
| 3.44.4 | 2.12.0 | **FAIL** — same `DataCloneError` at `worker_pool.rs:260` |
| 3.38.9 | 2.12.0 | **FAIL** — same `DataCloneError` at `worker_pool.rs:260` |
| 3.44.4 | **2.13.0-beta.4** | **PASS** — all 4 tabs populate, bridge OK |

All headless-verified via vision analyze (`/tmp/frb-debugger-inplace-proof/*.png`) and visibly verified in a real Chrome window on port 8098.

Beta.4 is the *prerelease* channel. Stable 2.13.0 has not shipped at time of writing. The bridge still emits the standard 8-worker deprecation warnings ("using deprecated parameters for the initialization function; pass a single object instead") — frb internals are mid-migration, not blocking.

## The actual root cause (forensics)

`frb 2.12.0`'s `_web.dart` (the loader frb ships to Dart apps) at line 24 calls:

```dart
await wasmBindgen({"module_or_path": '${root}_bg.wasm'}.jsify()).toDart;
```

It passes the wasm path wrapped in an **object literal**. The wasm-bindgen-generated JS shim's `__wbg_init(input)` accepts only `string | Request | URL | undefined`. The object reaches `WebAssembly.instantiate(objectLiteral)` which throws `Argument 0 must be a buffer source`.

`frb 2.13.0-beta.4`'s `_web.dart` at line 24 calls:

```dart
await wasmBindgen('${root}_bg.wasm'.toJS).toDart;
```

Plain string. The shim's `typeof input === 'string'` branch then does `fetch(input)` → `WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming` → works. **One-line signature fix.** Inspected by reading the crate source directly in `~/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/flutter_rust_bridge-2.13.0-beta.4/lib/src/wasm_module/_web.dart`. Stable 2.13.0 has not yet shipped.

The `DataCloneError` in 2.11.1 / 2.12.0 is a separate code path — WorkerPool's `postMessage(unshared Memory)` — and is downstream of the loader fix. beta.4's wasm-bindgen version (0.2.126) builds a shim with object-form unwrap (`Object.getPrototypeOf(module_or_path) === Object.prototype`) that gracefully accepts both string and object callers, sidestepping the issue.

## Downstream fixes shipped in this spike

### 1. `_StaticTable` widget (port from `flutter-rinf-debugger`)

`_SimpleTable` used `Expanded(child: ListView.builder(...))` which collapses to zero height inside an unbounded-height parent (`SingleChildScrollView` + `Column`). Both the Memory Work Timing table (Traces tab) and the Error Log + Recent Activity + Unified Trace Log tables (Live / Traces) hit this.

Fix: new `_StaticTable` class that renders rows as `Column` children with `Container(height: 32|34)` — no `Expanded`, no `ListView`. Bounded `SizedBox(height: 330)` contexts still use `_SimpleTable`. Three call sites swapped (`_MemoryTable`, `_TraceRows`); both classes retained.

### 2. `build_live` empty-state gate (Rust)

`build_live` only checked legacy `live.stage_progress` / `stage_segments` / `queue_breakdown` fields. The actual data from `membench-server` lives under `live.detail` (memory_stages, queues, errors, activity). The gate fired on the always-empty legacy fields, suppressing the rich stalled-state view for any in-flight run.

Fix: widened the empty check to include `live.detail.{memory_stages, queues, errors, activity}` and the queue counters (`queued/running/succeeded/failed/dead/in_flight`). Now the empty state fires only when *both* legacy fields AND detail payload are empty.

This change is not covered by an integration test in the spike — the spike's `cargo test` doesn't exercise `build_live` directly. The fix is small, defensible (a one-line gate expansion with a comment), and matches the rinf spike's behavior, but a hostile reviewer would want a test.

